-The CLI bundles Screenplay 4.226.0 (including its MCP server), Stage 4.178.2, and the Arc source adapter 22.54.0. `cratis render` admits ESM v1 through v30, including the canonical screen-composition corpus observable query and query-only specification shapes, and preserves authored Scene layouts, profiles, templates, navigation and forms when a model declares screens. Guarded screen actions render as runnable Scene guards: the generated frontend evaluates the authored guard, including enum-typed comparisons against the read model's declared members, and shows the action only when it passes. The renderer still refuses unsupported constructs within those versions: captures, non-event triggers and Translate slices report `STAGE-ESM-024`; supported event-triggered Automation slices render, while reactions mixing event production and command invocation report `STAGE-ESM-037`, read-model absence assertions report `STAGE-ESM-027`, and unsupported v9 and v10 constructs report the codes listed in the admission table below. Reaction system identities and reaction/reducer observer filters render within their supported subset. It also refuses an evolved event until Stage can render its event-type migrations. A refused model lists every independent refusal in one render, so fixing it does not reveal new refusals one render at a time; a refusal by the target profile or an unaudited ESM version is still reported first. Validation rejects `numbers exact` (`PLAY0268`) and `implementation` attachments on concept, built-in, and whole-command rules.
+The CLI bundles Screenplay 4.232.0 (including its MCP server), Stage 4.178.2, and the Arc source adapter 22.54.0. `cratis render` admits ESM v1 through v30, including the canonical screen-composition corpus observable query and query-only specification shapes, and preserves authored Scene layouts, profiles, templates, navigation and forms when a model declares screens. Guarded screen actions render as runnable Scene guards: the generated frontend evaluates the authored guard, including enum-typed comparisons against the read model's declared members, and shows the action only when it passes. The renderer still refuses unsupported constructs within those versions: captures, non-event triggers and Translate slices report `STAGE-ESM-024`; supported event-triggered Automation slices render, while reactions mixing event production and command invocation report `STAGE-ESM-037`, read-model absence assertions report `STAGE-ESM-027`, and unsupported v9 and v10 constructs report the codes listed in the admission table below. Reaction system identities and reaction/reducer observer filters render within their supported subset. It also refuses an evolved event until Stage can render its event-type migrations. A refused model lists every independent refusal in one render, so fixing it does not reveal new refusals one render at a time; a refusal by the target profile or an unaudited ESM version is still reported first. Validation rejects `numbers exact` (`PLAY0268`) and `implementation` attachments on concept, built-in, and whole-command rules.
 
 Stage 4.154.1 renders a two-project solution: the web application and a separate `<Project>.Specs` project that compiles the slice-local specifications. Generated applications use central package management, `Directory.Build.props`, and a README with run instructions, with Arc 22.112.1 and Chronicle 19.78.0.
 
